// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/order_presentation.t27 -- what a customer is told about an order that is theirs
; This contract owns three questions and nothing else: which STATUS a customer is shown for an
; order of theirs, which FIGURES they are shown, and what they are shown when either one is
; missing. The boundary is the two screens the customer reaches with their own identity --
; src/ui/screens/orders_screen.rs (the list and its four filter chips) and
; src/ui/screens/order_detail_screen.rs (one order in full) -- plus the rendering consequences
; of the component they share, src/ui/components/status_stepper.rs, whose pipeline CONTENT
; belongs to turbobaby/order-status and is not restated here.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-22: the boundary gained a fourth file that day, src/trios/order_status_view.rs,
; the one reading of the status string that the two screens and the stepper now share. It is
; owned here and compiled on the host. The pipeline it declares is still turbobaby/order-status's
; CONTENT: host tests in that module pin it to the order-status declarations, and nothing here
; restates it.
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-21). 996 lines of this tree are named by no contract at all: 440 in the
; orders list and 556 in the order detail screen. They are not leftovers awaiting retirement and
; they are not design-system primitives -- they are the last surface between the server's order
; row and the person who paid for it, and everything on them is a sentence addressed to that
; person. Four measurements taken while reading those 996 lines say why one contract had to cover
; both files at once. FIRST: one status string is read by FIFTEEN decision sites across the three
; files, SIX of which lower-case it first and NINE of which compare it raw, so the label a
; customer is shown and the filter chip they find it under are decided by two different readings
; of the same word. SECOND: the status label table holds EIGHT keys for the server's NINE accepted
; names, and the missing one is not an oversight -- there is no T_ORDERS_STATUS_COMPLETED constant
; anywhere in src/trios/i18n.rs (the eight are declared at src/trios/i18n.rs:472-479), so the
; alias pair turbobaby/order-status records is invisible to a customer by construction. THIRD:
; the stepper resolves a status name it does not carry to the index AFTER the last step
; (UNRESOLVED_INDEX_RULE_SITE_BEFORE_REPAIR below) and fills a segment whenever its index is at or
; below the current one (SEGMENT_FILL_RULE_SITE_BEFORE_REPAIR below), so a status this software
; does not understand renders as a COMPLETED delivery -- absence rendered as the most reassuring
; thing on the screen. FOURTH: of the FIVE money figures that reach these screens, exactly ONE
; passes through the published/dash filter D9 requires; the other four go straight into
; crate::trios::pricing::format_baht, whose sanitize_money (src/trios/pricing.rs:119-125) maps a
; non-finite or negative amount to 0.0. So a total nobody could compute is shown as a price.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-22, and the paragraph above is kept as the record of commit 14b01ac (the two
; stepper sites it named are now under _BEFORE_REPAIR names). FIRST and THIRD were repaired that
; day by one exact reading of the string, and so was the raw server token printed as a step
; label, which the 2026-09-21 reading had seen only for names nobody recognised: it reached every
; cancelled and every rejected order too. SECOND stands: the eight keys are unchanged, and adding
; either missing label is a decision the owner has not made (COMPLETED_KEY_AWAITS_THE_OWNER,
; REJECTED_KEY_AWAITS_THE_OWNER). FOURTH belongs to the money family and is not touched by the
; repair. The census of copies OUTSIDE this boundary was wrong and is corrected where it sits.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-22, the money repair: FOURTH is repaired on the two screens, and its cause is
; corrected. Every one of the five figures now passes an absence-aware decision (four of them in
; src/trios/pricing.rs, which the host tests), no order figure reaches format_baht bare, absence
; has one shape on both screens -- the dash -- and a payload missing a figure no longer loses
; either screen. But sanitize_money was never the zero a customer could see: both order endpoints
; send the row through one conversion that substitutes 0.0 for an unusable stored figure, and JSON
; cannot carry NaN or infinity. For the payloads the shipped server sends, one figure renders
; differently after the repair -- a zero subtotal, now a dash -- while the server's substituted
; zero on a total or a discount is still indistinguishable from a real one. D9 is therefore still
; not obeyed end to end; the figures section says exactly where.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-23, T27 defect 2 closed: the conversion now sends null for an unusable stored
; figure and names the field and the reason in the same response, every other reader of those
; payloads reads an absence first, and a figure nobody computed reaches the customer as the dash.
; The broad D9 flag still reads false, no longer for the wire: for owner question F, and because
; the committed dist/ predates the readers -- shipping this server before dist/ is rebuilt would
; lose screens. The figures section says exactly where (SHIPPING_THIS_SERVER_WITH_THE_COMMITTED_DIST_LOSES_SCREENS).
; CORRECTED 2026-09-24: dist/ is rebuilt in the same change that lands the wire fix, from the tree
; that carries every reader, so that release gap is closed; the broad D9 flag stays false for
; owner question F alone.
; --
; WHAT THIS FILE NEVER DOES. It holds no order id, no customer name, no phone number, no address
; and no delivery note (D14) -- not in a constant, not in a test argument, and not in an example.
; It publishes no user-facing copy and no Cyrillic: every string a customer reads is cited by the
; NAME of its i18n key and never by its text, and the key texts stay in the two tables
; turbobaby/locale-policy points at. It invents no status name for a state the server does not
; send: the eighth label is a label for the ABSENCE of a recognised name, not a ninth name, and
; nothing here adds a tenth. It does not restate the server vocabulary, the terminal set, the
; display pipeline, the money identity, the delivery figures or the locale tables -- those belong
; to the seven contracts named by ID below, and only booleans and cardinalities cross. Above all
; it RESOLVES NOTHING: the completed/delivered alias is turbobaby/order-status's question, and
; what is written here is only what the customer currently sees while that question is open. Where
; the screens have no rule -- a refused cancellation, an expired live view, an ETA the server keeps
; sending -- this file declares that there is none, and does not supply one.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-22: a status outside the vocabulary was on that list until the repair. It has
; had one rule since, the owner's DEFAULT recorded under UNREADABLE_PICTURE_IS_THE_OWNERS_DEFAULT:
; it is built from pieces the screens already shipped, it invents no copy and no number, and it
; is recorded here as an open question for the owner rather than as a ruling of this file.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-22, the cancel repair: a refused cancellation was on that list too, and the
; screen has had a rule for it since that day, recorded under "The two things a customer can DO".
; The rule is not this file's invention. Closing the dialog only on the server's confirmation is
; AGENTS.md lesson 4; looking at the order again before an attempt whose outcome is unknown is
; repeated is the owner's three-outcome rule for the bot, followed here because the Mini App has
; none of its own;
; and every sentence the customer reads about the attempt is the client-errors contract's. That
; contract is the eighth neighbour since the same day (REUSES_CLIENT_ERRORS_ID), so "the seven
; contracts named by ID below" now reads eight.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-22, the money repair: the screens have had a rule for an absent figure since
; that day, recorded in the figures section as the screens' own. It supplies nothing D9 does not
; already say -- absent renders as a dash -- and it takes each zero from the neighbour that owns
; it: a total's zero is a measurement because the order-money contract floors its identity at
; zero, and a subtotal's zero is a sum of line prices that the line total on the same card already
; calls absent. Two questions it does NOT answer are declared open instead of answered: which
; sentence, if any, stands beside a dashed order figure, and what an order holding a bike line
; should show as its total. The commerce contract, whose ledger the second touches, is the ninth
; neighbour since the same day (REUSES_COMMERCE_ID), so "the seven contracts named by ID below" now
; reads nine.
; ADDED 2026-09-25, the owner's answer 3: a fourth question, which NAME a customer is shown for a
; line of the old catalogue on an order of theirs, and which SHOP. The answer is the operator's
; neutral name, cited by its key like every other string here, and a withheld shop; the section
; "The name of a line of the old catalogue" says where both are decided and what they cost. The
; rule lives in src/trios/legacy_view.rs, a fifth file this boundary names without owning, and
; turbobaby/legacy-retirement, which records the answer, is named there (RETIRED_LINE_OWNER_ID) and
; is not counted among the nine neighbours: nothing of its is consumed but the date.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module turbobaby-order-presentation;

pub const KIND : str = "contract";
pub const ID : str = "turbobaby/order-presentation";
pub const NAME : str = "TurboBaby order presentation: what a customer is told about their order";
pub const WORLD : str = "gHashTag/turbobaby-user-bot";
; D13 joined on 2026-09-22 because the raw English server token the repair removed broke it, and
; D15 and D16 because the repair follows them: D15 by analogy (it is written for the price
; arithmetic, and names the hand-copied computation as this tree's recurring defect) and D16
; because every scan the repair added pins a floor.
pub const DECISIONS : [5]str = ["D9", "D13", "D14", "D15", "D16"];
pub const MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-21";
; The status repair. The code this file first measured is commit 14b01ac, and src/ at that
; commit is byte-identical to upstream main a33e500, so git show 14b01ac:PATH re-reads every site
; kept below under a _BEFORE_REPAIR name.
pub const STATUS_READING_REPAIRED_AT : str = "2026-09-22";
pub const PRE_REPAIR_COMMIT : str = "14b01ac";
; The cancel repair, the same day and on the same tree. Its _BEFORE_REPAIR sites are commit
; 14b01ac's too, like every other site kept under that suffix in this file.
pub const CANCEL_ANSWER_REPAIRED_AT : str = "2026-09-22";
; The money repair, the same day and on the same tree, and its _BEFORE_REPAIR sites are commit
; 14b01ac's as well.
pub const MONEY_REPAIRED_AT : str = "2026-09-22";

; --- The surface this file owns, by path and by size -------------------------------------------
; The two line counts are the measurement that forced this contract into existence; they are
; recorded so a later reader can re-run wc and see whether the surface has moved under the words.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-22: the repair moved every status decision out of the three UI files and into
; READING_IMPLEMENTATION, so all four counts changed. The 2026-09-21 values are kept below, and
; gate 3 now binds the current four to wc -l, because two more families edit the same screens.
pub const LIST_IMPLEMENTATION : str = "src/ui/screens/orders_screen.rs";
pub const DETAIL_IMPLEMENTATION : str = "src/ui/screens/order_detail_screen.rs";
pub const SHARED_COMPONENT : str = "src/ui/components/status_stepper.rs";
pub const READING_IMPLEMENTATION : str = "src/trios/order_status_view.rs";
; CORRECTED 2026-09-22 again, by the cancel repair: the detail screen went from 525 lines to 589
; when its cancellation started reading its answer (a handler prop, the reading of what landed
; since the answer, the line above the pending gate, and the sending task appended at the end).
; The two counts the status repair measured are kept under _AFTER_THE_STATUS_REPAIR names.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-22 a third time, by the money repair: the list went from 410 lines to 411 (its
; total became an Option carrying a default attribute) and the detail stayed at 589 (its four bare
; figures became a four-line flattened block, its three formatter calls a three-line call of the
; order rule). The counts the cancel repair left are kept under _AFTER_THE_CANCEL_REPAIR names.
pub const LIST_LINE_COUNT : u16 = 411;
pub const DETAIL_LINE_COUNT : u16 = 589;
pub const OWNED_LINE_COUNT : u16 = 1000;
pub const LIST_LINE_COUNT_AFTER_THE_STATUS_REPAIR : u16 = 410;
pub const OWNED_LINE_COUNT_AFTER_THE_CANCEL_REPAIR : u16 = 999;
pub const DETAIL_LINE_COUNT_AFTER_THE_STATUS_REPAIR : u16 = 525;
pub const OWNED_LINE_COUNT_AFTER_THE_STATUS_REPAIR : u16 = 935;
pub const SHARED_COMPONENT_LINE_COUNT : u16 = 72;
pub const READING_LINE_COUNT : u16 = 657;
pub const LIST_LINE_COUNT_BEFORE_REPAIR : u16 = 440;
pub const DETAIL_LINE_COUNT_BEFORE_REPAIR : u16 = 556;
pub const OWNED_LINE_COUNT_BEFORE_REPAIR : u16 = 996;
pub const SHARED_COMPONENT_LINE_COUNT_BEFORE_REPAIR : u16 = 122;
; The stepper stays a SHARED component and is not owned here as a file: what is owned is its
; rendering rule. Stated rather than implied since 2026-09-22, because that rule moved. The
; stepper now decides nothing itself -- it asks READING_IMPLEMENTATION, which IS owned here and
; is the one file of the four that the host compiles (src/lib.rs gates src/ui on wasm32).
pub const SHARED_COMPONENT_IS_OWNED_HERE : bool = false;
pub const SHARED_COMPONENT_DECIDES_NOTHING_ITSELF : bool = true;
pub const READING_IS_OWNED_HERE : bool = true;
pub const READING_IS_HOST_COMPILED : bool = true;

; And the boundary's honest edge, added by the review of 2026-09-21 because a contract named for
; what a customer is told about an order must not leave a reader believing two screens exhaust the
; subject. They do not. A THIRD customer surface renders the status of the customer's own last
; order -- src/ui/screens/home_screen.rs:320-322 computes its label, its colour and its total and
; :342 and :345 render them -- through a fourth copy of the same helper block. That file is owned
; by turbobaby/customer-surface and is not touched, measured or judged from here. What is declared
; is only that it exists, so the two counts of owned lines above read as a boundary and never as a
; census of where a customer meets an order status.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-22, two halves of that paragraph. "A fourth copy" counted the three copies
; inside this boundary, and none has been left inside it since the repair, so the home screen's
; block is now simply the first copy outside it. And the home screen is not the only other
; surface: the census further down (CUSTOMER_STATUS_SURFACES_OUTSIDE_THE_BOUNDARY) names four.
; What stays true is the ownership: none of those files is touched or judged from here, and no
; gate binds any of them to this contract -- the census below is a dated reading of where they
; are, not a measurement this file enforces.
pub const THIRD_CUSTOMER_SURFACE_SHOWS_AN_ORDER_STATUS : bool = true;
pub const THIRD_CUSTOMER_SURFACE_SITE : str = "src/ui/screens/home_screen.rs:320-322";
pub const THIRD_CUSTOMER_SURFACE_OWNER : str = "turbobaby/customer-surface";
pub const THIRD_CUSTOMER_SURFACE_IS_OWNED_HERE : bool = false;

; --- The neighbours, named by owner and by declaration (seven until 2026-09-22, nine since) ------
; There is no import in this language, so a REUSES_ string plus a test asserting it is the only
; way one contract can name another's territory. Each edge below is named by the owner's ID and,
; where this file consumes a specific fact, by the DECLARATION NAME it consumes -- never by a line
; number in the neighbour's file, which goes stale on that neighbour's next edit and says nothing
; when it does. What crosses every one of these edges is a boolean or a cardinality. No table,
; no vocabulary, no arithmetic and no price is copied across.
pub const REUSES_ORDER_STATUS_ID : str = "turbobaby/order-status";
pub const REUSES_ORDER_MONEY_ID : str = "turbobaby/order-money";
pub const REUSES_PRICING_HONESTY_ID : str = "turbobaby/pricing-honesty";
pub const REUSES_LOCALE_POLICY_ID : str = "turbobaby/locale-policy";
pub const REUSES_DELIVERY_TERMS_ID : str = "turbobaby/delivery-terms";
pub const REUSES_DEEPLINK_ID : str = "turbobaby/deeplink";
pub const REUSES_WEBAPP_BRIDGE_ID : str = "turbobaby/webapp-bridge";
; The eighth, added 2026-09-22 with the cancel repair. What a customer is told when something
; fails -- and the rule that a failure is never told as nothing -- is the client-errors contract's,
; and the cancellation became its third surface that day. This file owns WHETHER the answer is
; told and when the dialog, the offer and the re-read happen; which sentence each answer gets is
; consumed by declaration name and never restated.
pub const REUSES_CLIENT_ERRORS_ID : str = "turbobaby/client-errors";
; The ninth, added 2026-09-22 with the money repair. Which lines an order's stored sums include --
; and that a rental's money lives in its deal and not in them -- is the ledger of the commerce
; contract. This file names it only to say why the total of an order holding a bike line is an
; open owner question (BIKE_LINE_ORDER_TOTAL_NOTE); no rule of commerce's is restated here.
pub const REUSES_COMMERCE_ID : str = "turbobaby/commerce";
pub const NEIGHBOUR_COUNT : u8 = 9;
pub const NEIGHBOUR_COUNT_BEFORE_THE_MONEY_REPAIR : u8 = 8;
pub const NEIGHBOUR_COUNT_BEFORE_THE_CANCEL_REPAIR : u8 = 7;
pub const CLIENT_ERRORS_EDGE_ADDED_AT : str = "2026-09-22";
pub const COMMERCE_EDGE_ADDED_AT : str = "2026-09-22";
pub const NEIGHBOURS : [9]str = [
  "turbobaby/order-status",
  "turbobaby/order-money",
  "turbobaby/pricing-honesty",
  "turbobaby/locale-policy",
  "turbobaby/delivery-terms",
  "turbobaby/deeplink",
  "turbobaby/webapp-bridge",
  "turbobaby/client-errors",
  "turbobaby/commerce",
];
pub const VOCABULARY_DECLARATION : str = "STATUS_NAMES and STATUS_COUNT, declared by the order-status contract";
pub const TERMINALITY_DECLARATION : str = "order_status_is_terminal, declared by the order-status contract";
pub const ALIAS_DECLARATION : str = "ALIAS_ACCEPTED_NAME and ALIAS_PERSISTED_NAME, declared by the order-status contract";
pub const PIPELINE_LENGTH_DECLARATION : str = "DISPLAY_PIPELINE_VARIANT_COUNT, declared by the order-status contract";
pub const PIPELINE_GAP_DECLARATION : str = "DISPLAY_PIPELINE_MISSING_NAMES, declared by the order-status contract";
pub const CANCEL_PRECONDITION_DECLARATION : str = "order_status_customer_cancel_admitted, declared by the order-status contract";
