; by an unrecognised name, but the step label had no arm for cancelled or rejected either, so
; EVERY cancelled and every rejected card printed the English server word in both locales -- the
; common path, and a D13 breach (Russian is primary). And for those two names the token was the
; ONLY thing on screen that told a rejected order from a cancelled one. Since the repair no step
; label is ever the server's string; an arm with no step shows no step, so the two now look alike
; on these screens until the owner rules on question B.
