; --- The figures, and the four different things absence looked like ----------------------------
; Five money figures reach these two screens. ONE of them -- the per-line total at
; src/ui/screens/order_detail_screen.rs:162-166 -- goes through the published filter and renders a
; dash when the shop never priced the line, which is what D9 requires and what the
; pricing-honesty contract calls SHAPE_DASH. The other four go directly into format_baht, which
; takes a plain f64 and cannot express absence: src/trios/pricing.rs:119-125 turns a non-finite or
; negative amount into 0.0 first. So the answer to "does this screen obey D9" is: on the line it
; does, on the order it does not, and the two sit four lines apart in the same card.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-22, the money repair, in four parts. (1) The paragraph above is the record of
; commit 14b01ac, and its four sites are kept under UNFILTERED_SITES_BEFORE_REPAIR (that commit's
; lines). Since the repair every one of the five figures passes an absence-aware decision: the line
; total through the published filter as before, the other four through the order rule in
; src/trios/pricing.rs (ORDER_FIGURE_FILTER, ORDER_FIGURE_RENDERERS), which the host compiles and
; tests. Gate 3 counts format_baht on both screens at zero (DETAIL_FORMAT_BAHT_OCCURRENCE_COUNT,
; LIST_FORMAT_BAHT_OCCURRENCE_COUNT). (2) The causal attribution above was wrong for every payload
; the shipped server can send. Both order endpoints serialise the row through one conversion
; (ORDER_ENDPOINTS_SERIALISE_THROUGH_ONE_CONVERSION) that substitutes 0.0 for a stored figure that
; is not finite and non-negative (WIRE_ZERO_SUBSTITUTION_SITE) and clamps the star count at zero
; (WIRE_STAR_CLAMP_SITE), and JSON cannot carry NaN or infinity at all. So sanitize_money was
; reachable from these screens only through a negative number the server never sends, and the
; zero a customer could actually see was the server's.
; (3) Hence D9 is still NOT obeyed on these screens end to end, and the constant below stays false
; with a narrower true one beside it (EVERY_FIGURE_PASSES_THE_SCREEN_FILTER). For the payloads the
; shipped server sends today exactly one figure renders differently after the repair: a zero
; subtotal, which is now a dash (ZERO_SUBTOTAL_RENDERS_AS_A_DASH). Everything else the repair
; changes is for a payload the server cannot yet send -- a figure missing or null -- and that is
; the precondition for the server ever saying "absent" (WIRE_ZERO_NOTE). (4) "Calls SHAPE_DASH" is
; narrowed: the glyph is the one the catalog renders for that contract's SHAPE_DASH (the component
; layer's DASH), but that contract scopes the sentence its SHAPE_DASH carries to one value, the
; per-day rate of a bike family (DASH_SENTENCE_DECLARATION). No sentence travels with a dash on these screens, the line's
; included, and whether one should is the owner's open question (ORDER_FIGURE_DASH_NOTE).
; CORRECTED 2026-09-23, T27 defect 2 closed on the wire, in four parts. (1) The conversion no longer
; substitutes. A stored subtotal, bonus_used or total that is not finite and non-negative, and a
; negative star count, leave src/db/orders.rs as null (WIRE_WITHHOLD_SITE, WIRE_STAR_WITHHOLD_SITE),
; and the same response names each withheld field under MONEY_WITHHELD_FIELD with the one reason
; that exists (MONEY_WITHHELD_REASON); the log line keeps the order id and the stored value. The
; comment that justified the zero was wrong twice: the wire field is not the NOT NULL column, and
; serde_json writes a NaN as null instead of failing. The sites the paragraphs above cite are kept
; under _BEFORE_THE_WIRE_FIX names (the numbering of a33e500, which this file equalled until then).
; (2) The precondition WIRE_ZERO_NOTE named is met in the same change: every other reader of these
; payloads reads an absence first (ABSENCE_READING_SITES) -- the home widget and the profile history
; print their total through order_total_text, the admin card, badges and CSV through the same
; measured filter, and the webapp-bridge mirror declares an Option. The two admin endpoints go
; through the same conversion (ADMIN_ENDPOINTS_SERIALISE_THROUGH_THE_SAME_CONVERSION), which the
; 2026-09-22 reading left out. (3) Hence, in the source tree, a figure nobody computed reaches the
; customer as the dash (A_FIGURE_NOBODY_COMPUTED_REACHES_THE_CUSTOMER_AS_THE_DASH), the one shape of
; absence the screens can now meet -- that is defect 2, closed. The broad D9 constant still reads
; false, and no longer for the wire. First, a bike-only order stores a finite zero the server
; cannot tell from a real one and it prints as a price (BIKE_LINE_ORDER_TOTAL_NOTE, owner question
; F). Second, see (4). No sentence travels with the dash (ORDER_FIGURE_DASH_NOTE, owner question
; E): the reason is named in the response and the log, not yet in words a customer reads. (4) The
; client that ships is the committed dist/ (SHIPPED_CLIENT_SOURCE), built before these readers
; changed and holding bare numbers in every one of them, the serde default included (it covers a
; missing key, not a null). Shipping this server before dist/ is rebuilt would turn one withheld
; figure into a lost order list, detail, home widget, profile history and admin page -- worse than
; the zero it removes (SHIPPING_THIS_SERVER_WITH_THE_COMMITTED_DIST_LOSES_SCREENS). That is recorded,
; not gated: nothing in CI rebuilds dist/ (SHIPPED_CLIENT_REBUILT_WITH_THIS_CHANGE). CORRECTED
; 2026-09-24: the landing change rebuilt dist/ through scripts/build-frontend.sh from the tree that
; carries every reader and passed scripts/predeploy-smoke.sh --no-build, so the committed client
; reads an absence and the screens are not lost; the two facts above keep their 2026-09-23 values
; under the _BEFORE_THE_REBUILD names. Still not gated in CI. Proved on the host by the unit test
; an_unusable_stored_figure_is_never_shown_as_a_price in src/db/orders.rs: red before the change (a
; stored NaN total printed as a zero price), green after.
