; Absence had four different shapes here, and which one a customer got depended on which field
; went missing rather than on any rule. The fourth is the loudest and the least expected: the
; order totals are declared as plain numbers -- three f64 and one i64 -- with no serde default
; (src/ui/screens/order_detail_screen.rs:33-36 at 14b01ac), so a payload that omits one does not
; render a dash or a zero -- deserialization fails and the customer is told the order was not found.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-22, the money repair, in three parts. (1) The 2026-09-21 reading named only the
; detail screen. The list declared its total the same way (src/ui/screens/orders_screen.rs:27 at
; 14b01ac), and there one order without a total failed the WHOLE response, so every order vanished
; behind the error text (LIST_LOST_EVERY_ORDER_BEFORE_REPAIR). (2) Since the repair every figure is
; an Option carrying #[serde(default)] (OPTIONAL_FIGURE_SITES): the detail flattens the order rule's
; own block, the list declares its total as one. That is the shape the webapp-bridge contract's own
; rule counts as neither breaking the client nor inventing a value (MISSING_FIELD_DECLARATION), so
; this file and that one agree on it. A missing or null figure is an absence and renders as the
; dash. (3) The shape count is split, because the two readings differ. What the SCREENS render for
; an absence they can see is one shape, the dash. What a CUSTOMER can meet is three, before the
; repair and after it: the dash, and the server's substituted zero, which prints as a zero on a
; total and omits a discount row (WIRE_ZERO_NOTE). The lost screen was never reachable through the
; shipped server, which sends all four figures on every row; it is gone all the same.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-23, T27 defect 2: the server no longer substitutes a zero (WIRE_WITHHOLD_SITE),
; so the two customer-only shapes are gone and what a CUSTOMER can meet is one, the dash, the same
; count the screens render. The three stays on record as the count before the wire fix. Both counts
; describe the source tree: with the committed dist/ a withheld figure loses the screen instead
; (SHIPPING_THIS_SERVER_WITH_THE_COMMITTED_DIST_LOSES_SCREENS). CORRECTED 2026-09-24: the rebuilt
; dist/ is built from that source tree, so both counts now describe the committed client too.
; What still loses a screen is named rather than implied: a field that is not money and is declared
; bare -- the order's id, items, status and created_at, and each line's quantity -- and a figure of
; another JSON type, such as a star count sent as a fraction.
pub const FIGURE_SHOWN : u8 = 0;
pub const ABSENCE_RENDERS_AS_DASH : u8 = 1;
pub const ABSENCE_RENDERS_AS_ZERO : u8 = 2;
pub const ABSENCE_RENDERS_AS_OMITTED_ROW : u8 = 3;
pub const ABSENCE_RENDERS_AS_A_LOST_SCREEN : u8 = 4;
; Not an absence: a discount of zero is a measurement ("none applied"), and its row is omitted. It
