; --- The name of a line of the old catalogue (owner, 2026-09-25, answer 3) ----------------------
; DECIDED 2026-09-25. The owner's answer 3 of that day's second numbered list rules that what the
; previous shop left in storage leaves customers' sight, and that no stored row is deleted or
; rewritten for it; turbobaby/legacy-retirement records the answer (OWNER_ANSWER_3_AT) and the
; other reads it moved. On these screens that content is the order LINE. An order placed before
; migration 083 stores the old catalogue's lines -- a strain, an accessory, a tea or a set, each
; by id and by name -- and the list, the detail and the profile's recent orders printed each
; line's stored name as it was stored. The operator chose the neutral name those lines are shown
; under; like every string on this surface it is cited by its key, RETIRED_LINE_NAME_KEY, and its
; two rows are pinned by a host test beside the rule (RETIRED_LINE_UNIT_TESTS_LIVE_IN).
;
; THE RULE is the server's, so a bundle that predates it is served the neutral name too
; (customer_order_line in RETIRED_LINE_RULE). A line whose bike is not an object is of a retired
; kind, and it is served as at most three fields: the neutral name, under the one name field every
; owned screen reads first (RETIRED_LINE_NAME_FIELD), and its quantity and unit price exactly as
; stored (RETIRED_LINE_KEPT_FIELDS) -- a figure is copied, never judged or filled in, and D9 stays
; the screens' as above. Its ids, kind flags and service choice are not served, and neither is a
; key this repository never declared, so no reorder can rebuild the old item in a cart: all five
; reorder conversions (the three owned screens, home and success) drop a line with no id, which is
; what they already did, and home and success print no line name. A bike line is served
; as stored. The server writes the name in the language the stored names were written in
; (Russian), and each owned screen prints it through the same table in the reader's language
; (shown_line_name, RETIRED_LINE_PRINT_SITES), so a customer reading English reads the English row.
; Only the two customer reads apply the rule, through Order::for_customer; the admin reads keep
; the stored row, which is the archive.
;
; THE SHOP. The same two reads withhold the shop an order names when it names the previous shop
; (customer_shop_id); every shop value the old checkout stored did. A withheld shop reaches the
; keyless shop fallback both owned screens print for an absent shop (two of
; KEYLESS_CUSTOMER_STRING_SITES), and that fallback names THIS shop, so an order the previous shop
; took now reads as placed with this one, on the detail's labelled delivery row too. No neutral
; shop wording was given and none is supplied here (RETIRED_SHOP_FALLBACK_NOTE).
; DECIDED 2026-09-26, by the operator, announced to the owner with no objection: an order of the
; previous shop must NOT be shown as this shop's. No wording was needed, because the decision is to
; show no shop label at all for such an order. So a withheld shop is served as an EMPTY shop
; (RETIRED_SHOP_SERVED_AS; WITHHELD_SHOP in the rules' module), never as null: null is what an
; order naming no shop is served, and those keep the fallback. Each owned screen reads the served
; shop through shown_shop and prints no shop label for the empty one -- the list prints the date
; alone where it printed the shop and the date, and the detail leaves out its labelled delivery row,
; label and value -- while an order of this shop prints its stored shop, and one naming no shop the
; keyless fallback, exactly as before; the two fallback sites keep their literal on their cited
; lines, so KEYLESS_CUSTOMER_STRING_SITES holds, and no cited line moved. A bundle built before the
; decision prints an empty value for the empty shop: not this shop's name either. The Mini App's
; checkout never sends an empty shop, so no order of this shop is read as a withheld one.
;
; WHAT DID NOT MOVE. No status, no figure, no owner question above and no cited line: each of the
; three print sites was replaced in place, so LIST_LINE_COUNT and DETAIL_LINE_COUNT hold.
pub const RETIRED_LINE_DECIDED_AT : str = "2026-09-25";
pub const RETIRED_LINE_DECIDED_BY : str = "operator, applying the owner's answer 3 of 2026-09-25";
pub const RETIRED_LINE_OWNER_ID : str = "turbobaby/legacy-retirement";
pub const RETIRED_LINE_NAME_KEY : str = "T_ORDER_LINE_PREVIOUS_CATALOGUE";
pub const RETIRED_LINE_NAME_FIELD : str = "strain_name";
pub const RETIRED_LINE_KEPT_FIELD_COUNT : u8 = 2;
pub const RETIRED_LINE_KEPT_FIELDS : [2]str = ["quantity", "unit_price"];
