; "Refusal" in the constant below is the SHOP'S refusal -- rejected shares ARM_CANCELLED_OR_REJECTED
; -- and not a refused cancellation, which the paragraph above now also calls a refusal. What a
; refused cancellation offers is the sibling after it: whatever the DISPLAYED status offers. After
; a successful re-read that is the status the refusal found; after a failed one it is the loaded
; status again, and the loaded status can be stale.
pub const REORDER_IS_OFFERED_AFTER_A_REFUSAL : bool = true;
